flowchart TD
  A[Accepted Builder selection and production request\nOriginal Application / Page / node / committed hash] --> B[Real server rebinds original session and owner\nExisting authority; new qualified admission/invalidation adapter]
  B --> C[D6 recovery-free graph and role admission\nProposed source contract; no recovery or lock stealing]
  C --> D[Owner-controlled coherent byte and membership capture\nPage roles / required identity membership / pinned native package / theme policy]
  D --> E[Validate closed inputs and recheck source plus authority\nImmutable content identity separate from authority epoch]
  E --> F[Authenticated immutable capture/resource delivery\nFresh authority on every disclosure; approved bounds]
  F --> G[Production lifecycle adapter to admitted L3 native host\nPreserve source identity AND canonical Card identity]
  G --> H[Select real saved Card, click Preview\nRender actual captured Card with unchanged native renderer]
  B -. denied / unknown .-> U[Unavailable; no source fallback or demo rendering]
  C -. busy / unresolved / recovery required .-> U
  D -. missing / changed / ambiguous / unsupported .-> U
  E -. stale / revoked / unqualified .-> U
  F -. invalid resource / expired / unhealthy .-> U
  G -. source change / authority loss / lifecycle uncertainty .-> U
  R1[First recommended authorization\nRecovery-free read contract in existing Foundation owner\nSource changes plus isolated tests only] -. required before protected qualification .-> C
  O[Separate narrow D6 operational decision\nNamed roots and complete closure; real read authority\nOwn coordination metadata only; no recovery] -. required qualification .-> D
